                <pb facs="0576" n="462" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg462"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">706.6193/21: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-09-12T14:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 12,
                                1924—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 12—10:47
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>340. My 333, September 8, 4 p.m. French Minister agreed. We have accepted
                    Karakhan’s note of August 26th, sent him our acknowledgment, and he entered into
                    possession of former Russian Legation noon today. He will not occupy it for two
                    or three weeks as it needs cleaning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
